# TD GAMES Platform — App Launcher Architecture

Build the **TD GAMES** ecosystem as a single platform with an iPhone-style **Home Screen** after login. Each module is an independent "app" with its own icon, UI, and data.

## Architecture Overview

```
Login → Home Screen (App Grid) → Click App → Full App View (with ← Back)
```

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Login Screen] --> B[🏠 Home Screen]
    B --> C[📄 Invoice App]
    B --> D[💰 Expense App]
    B --> E[📊 Dashboard App - future]
    B --> F[... more apps]
    C --> B
    D --> B
    E --> B
```

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Home Screen replaces the old Navbar tabs**
> After login, user lands on a beautiful Home Screen with app icons in a grid. The Navbar module-switcher idea is scrapped. Each app has its own internal Navbar with a ← Back button.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **App Registry Pattern**
> Apps are registered in a simple array config. Adding a new app in the future = adding 1 entry to the config + the app component. Very extensible.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Platform Shell (Home Screen + App Router)

#### [NEW] `components/HomeScreen.tsx`
- Beautiful grid layout of app icons (like iPhone)
- Each app card: icon (emoji/SVG), name, brief description
- Dark theme matching existing design (`#0F0F0F` background)
- Smooth animations on hover/click
- Shows user info + logout button at top
- Initial apps:
  - 📄 **Invoice** — "Quản lý hoá đơn & doanh thu"
  - 💰 **Expense** — "Quản lý chi phí & thanh toán"

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/App.tsx)
- Add `activeApp` state: `null` (home) | `'invoice'` | `'expense'`
- `activeApp === null` → render `<HomeScreen />`
- `activeApp === 'invoice'` → render existing Invoice module
- `activeApp === 'expense'` → render new Expense module
- Pass `onBack={() => setActiveApp(null)}` to each app

#### [MODIFY] [Navbar.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/Navbar.tsx)
- Add a ← **Back to Home** button (left side) when inside an app
- Keep existing tab navigation for each app's internal tabs
- Show current app name in the navbar title area

#### [NEW] `config/apps.ts`
- App registry config array:
```ts
export const APPS = [
  { id: 'invoice', name: 'Invoice', icon: '📄', desc: 'Quản lý hoá đơn & doanh thu', color: '#FF9500' },
  { id: 'expense', name: 'Expense', icon: '💰', desc: 'Quản lý chi phí & thanh toán', color: '#34C759' },
  // Future: { id: 'dashboard', name: 'Dashboard', icon: '📊', ... }
];
```

